  "codex.safety": "Keep the forks low and the load tilted back while travelling|Never travel with a raised load — lower it before moving off|Sound the horn at blind corners, gate lanes and pedestrian walkways|Give way to pedestrians: they have priority over every machine|Observe the capacity chart: capacity falls as the boom reaches out|Never walk or stand under a suspended load|Come to a full stop before raising or lowering the attachment|Report every impact, however small, at the end of the shift",
  "codex.glossary": "TEU — twenty-foot equivalent unit, the standard measure of container traffic|Spreader — the frame that locks onto a container's four corner castings|Twistlock — the rotating pin that secures the spreader to the container|Bay, row, tier — the three coordinates that locate a container in a stack|RTG — rubber-tyred gantry crane, used to stack and shuffle the yard|STS — ship-to-shore gantry crane, the quay crane that works the vessel|Reach stacker — a mobile handler with a telescopic boom and spreader|Luffing — raising or lowering a crane boom; it changes radius and capacity|Out-of-gauge — cargo that does not fit the standard container envelope|Reefer — a refrigerated container that must stay plugged into power",
